  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Delaware has $191M in federal contract obligations for FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer, obligating $92.9M. Contracting activity in Delaware includes 2,970 awards so far, with an average award size of $64.2K. Obligations are down 48.2% year over year. Fiscal-year comparisons show prior totals of $321M in FY21, $81.3M in FY22, $325M in FY23, $337M in FY24, and $368M in FY25. The top buying agencies after the Department of Defense are the Department of Veterans Affairs with $37.4M and the Department of Health and Human Services with $17.8M. The top vendors include CAESAR RODNEY SCHOOL DISTRICT with $15M and STONEWIN INTERNATIONAL, LLC with $14.8M. The largest industries by NAICS include Other Computer Related Services at $18.4M and Elementary and Secondary Schools at $15M. All figures are contract obligations and current-year totals are partial fiscal year to date.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in Delaware changed this year?",
        "body": "FY2026 to date obligations total $191M. Obligations are down 48.2% year over year, and FY25 obligations were $368M compared with FY26 obligations of $191M. Delaware has 2,970 awards so far, with an average award size of $64.2K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and industries account for the largest share of Delaware spending?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer with $92.9M, followed by the Department of Veterans Affairs at $37.4M and the Department of Health and Human Services at $17.8M. Other Computer Related Services leads industries at $18.4M, followed by Elementary and Secondary Schools at $15M and Petroleum Refineries at $14.9M."
      }
    ]
  },
